<title>BELGIUM: EU vets Fortis buy of MeesPierson.</title>
<headline>EU vets Fortis buy of MeesPierson.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it had started a routine probe into the acquisition of merchant bank MeesPierson NV by Belgian-Dutch insurance and banking group Fortis.</p>
<p>It said the deal was submitted for clearance on January 3 under the European Union's merger rules which ban creation or strengthening of dominant positions. The Commission has about a month from the notification date to clear the deal or start a full probe.</p>
<p>Fortis, which is owned by Fortis AG and Fortis Amev NV, said earlier this month it had sealed the take-over of MeesPierson from Dutch bank ABN AMRO for 2.5 billion guilders.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
</text>
